{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T13:26:16.419Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"54ac87379db6592d81af1cc6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-wlxf8f"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"CLI argv keeps one value silently when two spellings of one extension flag differ (--status-filter a -s b), while direct callers are refused with extension_option_spelling_conflict"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found by CodeRabbit on PR 1682 (pm-gh1665). The shared extension option normalizer now refuses two spellings of one declared flag with different values for PmClient.run, MCP and the test harness (extension_option_spelling_conflict). CLI argv dispatch still folds them through mergeAliasOptionKeys in src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts: for scalar flags the canonical value wins and the alias value is dropped without a refusal, so pm demo --status-filter open -s closed silently runs with open. The parse-time occurrences recorded by parseLooseCommandOptions carry enough information to apply the same conflict check before dispatch. Changing this alters CLI behavior for existing scripts that repeat a flag under two spellings, so it was deferred from the batch. Duplicate check: searched spelling conflict, alias folding, repeated flag values and short alias across all statuses; pm-kfq5 owns list accumulation across long/short occurrences, not scalar conflicts."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","cli","extensions","flags"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-07T13:26:16.419Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T13:26:16.419Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"CLI argv that supplies two spellings of one declared scalar extension flag with different values exits 2 with extension_option_spelling_conflict naming both spellings and the handler key; Equal values and list flags keep their current accumulation; A spec drives the built CLI with --long and -s spellings, with a negative control that restores silent folding"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Declare --status-filter with short -s, run pm demo --status-filter open -s closed --json"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"exit 2 extension_option_spelling_conflict"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"exit 0; the handler receives statusFilter open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.11.7"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"extensions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1665","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-07T13:26:16.419Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-kfq5","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-07T13:26:16.419Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"257d9170e1eebced4f86877f86b79042e019552c7d0ebd01c52